### ext3 (.103) session count today (fix the missing probe)
grep "192.168.2.103" /var/log/cameras.log | grep -oE "session [0-9]+" | sort -u | wc -l
### ext2 (.105): the ONE BackchannelStreamState line today -- when?
grep "192.168.2.105" /var/log/cameras.log | grep "BackchannelStreamState" | grep "Sep 16"
### ext2 (.105): session ids today with timestamps (10 sessions = reconnects)
grep "192.168.2.105" /var/log/cameras.log | grep -oE "^Sep 16 [0-9:]+ .*session [0-9]+" | sed -E "s/.*(Sep 16 [0-9:]+).*session ([0-9]+)/\1 \2/" | sort -u | head -12
### ext3 (.103): BackchannelStreamState lines TODAY 10-min buckets
grep "192.168.2.103" /var/log/cameras.log | grep "BackchannelStreamState" | grep "^Sep 16" | awk '{print substr($3,1,5)}' | sort | uniq -c | tail -30
### ext2 (.105) vs ext3 (.103): cameras.log is syslog sink -- does .105 log prudynt INFO at all?
grep "192.168.2.105" /var/log/cameras.log | grep "prudynt" | grep "^Sep 16" | head -5